  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    results = []\n    for border_val in set(v for row in grid for v in row if v != 0):\n        cells = set()\n        for r in range(rows):\n            for c in range(cols):\n                if grid[r][c] == border_val:\n                    cells.add((r, c))\n        \n        for r1 in range(rows):\n            for c1 in range(cols):\n                if (r1, c1) not in cells:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1+2, rows):\n                    for c2 in range(c1+2, cols):\n                        valid = True\n                        for c in range(c1, c2+1):\n                            if (r1, c) not in cells or (r2, c) not in cells:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        for r in range(r1, r2+1):\n                            if (r, c1) not in cells or (r, c2) not in cells:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if valid:\n                            results.append((border_val, r1, c1, r2, c2, (r2-r1+1)*(c2-c1+1)))\n    \n    results.sort(key=lambda x: -x[5])\n    border_val, r1, c1, r2, c2, _ = results[0]\n    \n    other_val = 0\n    for r in range(r1+1, r2):\n        for c in range(c1+1, c2):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != border_val:\n                other_val = grid[r][c]\n                break\n        if other_val:\n            break\n    \n    out = []\n    for r in range(r1, r2+1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(c1, c2+1):\n            if grid[r][c] == border_val:\n                row.append(other_val)\n            else:\n                row.append(grid[r][c])\n        out.append(row)\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    results = []\n    for border_val in set(v for row in grid for v in row if v != 0):\n        cells = set()\n        for r in range(rows):\n            for c in range(cols):\n                if grid[r][c] == border_val:\n                    cells.add((r, c))\n        \n        for r1 in range(rows):\n            for c1 in range(cols):\n                if (r1, c1) not in cells:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1+2, rows):\n                    for c2 in range(c1+2, cols):\n                        valid = True\n                        for c in range(c1, c2+1):\n                            if (r1, c) not in cells or (r2, c) not in cells:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        for r in range(r1, r2+1):\n                            if (r, c1) not in cells or (r, c2) not in cells:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if valid:\n                            results.append((border_val, r1, c1, r2, c2, (r2-r1+1)*(c2-c1+1)))\n    \n    results.sort(key=lambda x: -x[5])\n    border_val, r1, c1, r2, c2, _ = results[0]\n    \n    other_val = 0\n    for r in range(r1+1, r2):\n        for c in range(c1+1, c2):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != border_val:\n                other_val = grid[r][c]\n                break\n        if other_val:\n            break\n    \n    out = []\n    for r in range(r1, r2+1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(c1, c2+1):\n            if grid[r][c] == border_val:\n                row.append(other_val)\n            else:\n                row.append(grid[r][c])\n        out.append(row)\n    return out",
